# Build context for the Selvedge MCP Catalog image.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST: deny everything, then re-admit exactly what
# `pip install .` needs. The wheel target is `packages = ["selvedge"]` and
# `readme = "README.md"` is read for package metadata at build time, so those
# four entries are the whole requirement.
#
# Why an allowlist rather than a deny list. A deny list has to be extended
# every time an internal-only file is added to the tree, and when someone
# forgets, it over-ships silently. This form fails the other way: anything not
# named below is simply absent, so a mistake breaks the build loudly instead of
# shipping something it shouldn't. It also keeps `.git` out, which is what
# keeps the whole history from landing in the image.
#
# The specific leak that motivated this: `.selvedge/` is git-tracked on purpose
# (Selvedge dogfoods itself), and `COPY . /app` with `WORKDIR /app` put the
# maintainer's store exactly where the entrypoint's walk-up DB resolution would
# select it — so the container served someone else's change history as its
# default state. Locally, `docker build .` also swept in `CLAUDE.local.md`,
# `internal/` and the rest of the git-excluded internal-ops material.
*
!selvedge/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# Re-exclude what could otherwise ride in under `selvedge/`. Docker's matcher
# is non-recursive, so these need the `**/` prefix to match at any depth — a
# bare `__pycache__` only ever matched the one at the context root.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.selvedge
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.DS_Store
